      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "HO1 requires verifying ambiguous findings and preventing both over-treatment and under-treatment. The doctor does this by explaining that a positive culture does not equal infection, and that antibiotic decisions must be based on clinical signs, not just the culture result. This is a beyond-minimum action that actively prevents both false-positive (overuse of antibiotics) and false-negative (ignoring infection) errors.",
